/-- **`S(3,2) ≤ 6`.**  The six multipliers `{1, 2, 4, 5, 7, 8}` hit every base-3
word of length two: for every irrational `α` and every pair `[a, b]` of base-3
digits, some `m ∈ {1,2,4,5,7,8}` has `[a, b]` occurring infinitely often in the
base-3 expansion of `m·α`. -/
